    rock: 'r2',
    item: 'LinkedIn content templates',
    title: 'LinkedIn content templates',
    prompt: `Write a set of reusable LinkedIn post templates for Livly's content team, organized by format. Include:\n\n(1) Thought leadership post (for David Shaw) — structure: provocative opening statement, 3-5 short punchy paragraphs building the argument, landing with a reframe or call to think differently. 150–200 words. No bullet lists. First person.\n\n(2) Product announcement post (for Livly page) — structure: problem statement in one sentence, product reveal in one sentence, 3 short bullets on what it does, social proof line, CTA. 100–130 words.\n\n(3) Event recap post (for Livly page or team) — structure: event name + outcome in first sentence, 2–3 key conversations or themes, gratitude or forward-looking close. 80–100 words.\n\n(4) Data/insight post (for any contributor) — structure: lead with the surprising number, explain what it means in one sentence, give the implication for operators, close with a question. 100–120 words.\n\n(5) Partnership announcement post — structure: announcement in first sentence, why this partnership matters to operators in 2 sentences, 2 bullets of joint value, CTA. 100–120 words.\n\nFor each template: include a fill-in structure with [brackets] for the specific content.`,
