    rock: 'r3',
    item: 'Build content-to-demo attribution tracking',
    title: 'Content-to-demo attribution',
    prompt: `Build a content-to-demo attribution system for Livly that connects LinkedIn and email content to inbound demo requests. We can't use UTM tracking on personal LinkedIn posts, so we need a practical attribution approach. Build: (1) the attribution model — how to credit content when someone books a demo after engaging with our LinkedIn or email, (2) the intake question to add to our demo booking form: "How did you hear about us?" with specific options that map to our content channels, (3) a manual attribution log — when someone books a demo, the 3 fields to fill in: content source, specific post or email, time lag between first touch and booking, (4) the weekly check — how to review inbound leads for content signals even when attribution is imperfect, (5) the end-of-quarter calculation — how to count "5 content-attributed demos" in a way that's honest and defensible even with partial attribution data.`,
